# PLAN1-RT — Ship 1 LSP completion runtime seal

File: openOODA/audit/plan1_rt.oot
Wave 0. Read only. No product edit. No runtime edit. No oodac edit.

Logline: This board proves product `ooda lsp` can add textDocument/completion with live C APIs only.
Setup: Read cli/lsp_reply.oo, cli/lsp_drive.oo, cli/lsp_ident.oo, and the unused catalog. Do not grow lsp/.
Beats:
  1. State the verdict.
  2. Map each needed .oo name to a live C API.
  3. Name emit fails that are import errors, not new C.

## 1. Verdict

no runtime change required
no oodac change required

Emit of new `cli/lsp_complete.oo` does not need a new C API.
Do not patch `chs_rt`. Do not patch `oodac`.
Do not add `oo_lsp_*`. Do not add a JSON parser in C.

Status: done for the runtime seal. Product write is still open.

## 2. Method

Proof is static. Seed emit already builds `bin/ooda` from `cli/main.oo`.
That tree already imports `lsp_drive.oo` → `lsp_reply.oo` → `lsp_ident.oo`.
The catalog uses the same names. Those names already lower to `chs_rt`.
A new same-folder import does not add a C symbol.

Worktree root is the ooda tree. There is no folder `ooda/lsp/`.
The unused catalog is `lsp/lsp_completion.oo`.
A copy sits at `cli/lsp/lsp_completion.oo`.
Plan words `ooda/lsp/` mean that unused `lsp/` tree. Do not grow it.

## 3. Product path today

`vscode` starts `bin/ooda lsp`. `cli/main.oo` calls `run_ooda_lsp`.
`cli/lsp_drive.oo` frames stdin and calls `lsp_build_reply`.
`cli/lsp_reply.oo` line 152 advertises hover, documentSymbol, and definition.
It does not advertise `completionProvider`.
It has no `textDocument/completion` branch.
Unknown methods return empty. `lsp_emit` skips an empty payload.

`cli/lsp_ident.oo` already reads `"line":` and `"character":`.
It maps them with `lsp_src_offset` and `lsp_ident_at`.
Hover and definition already use that path.
VS Code does not send a `"prefix"` key.

## 4. Unused catalog

`lsp/lsp_completion.oo` holds labels for caps, keywords, types, and builtins.
`lsp_completion_resolve` filters with a prefix string.
Empty prefix returns every item (`lsp_str_starts_with`, plen 0).
`&Fs` matches `&FsCap`, `&FsReadCap`, and `&FsWriteCap`.
The list has 30 items. The ship cap is 64.

`lsp/lsp_server.oo` line 60 reads a fake `"prefix"` key.
That is why the unused tree is wrong for VS Code.
DE2 must lift the catalog text into `cli/lsp_complete.oo`.
DE2 must not import `lsp/`. Same-folder imports only.

The catalog import of `lsp_types.oo` is unused in the resolve path.
Do not copy that import into `cli/` unless `cli/lsp_types.oo` exists.

## 5. Live C APIs

Seed `c_emit` already maps these names. `chs_rt.h` already declares them.
The product CLI already calls them.

| .oo name | C API | Live caller |
| --- | --- | --- |
| chars_len | oo_chars_len | cli/lsp_ident.oo |
| char_at | oo_char_at | cli/lsp_ident.oo |
| str_slice | oo_str_slice | cli/lsp_ident.oo |
| str_index_of | oo_str_index_of | cli/lsp_reply.oo |
| str_starts_with | oo_str_starts_with | cli/lsp_drive.oo |
| byte_at | oo_byte_at | cli/lsp_ident.oo |
| list_new | oo_slist_new | cli/main.oo |
| list_push | oo_slist_push | cli/main.oo |
| list_len | oo_slist_len | cli/main.oo |
| list_get | oo_slist_get | cli/main.oo |
| read_file | oo_read_file | cli/lsp_reply.oo |
| path_exists | oo_path_exists | cli/lsp_reply.oo |
| to_string | oo_int_to_str | cli/lsp_reply.oo |
| string + | oo_str_concat | cli/lsp_reply.oo |
| string lit | oo_str_lit | cli/lsp_reply.oo |

`c_emit_ty.oo` maps `List[String]` to `oo_slist_*`.
`c_emit_call.oo` maps `.to_string()` to `oo_int_to_str`.
`c_emit_libfloor.oo` maps `str_starts_with` and `str_index_of`.

Completion JSON is string concat. It is not a new parser.
Initialize is a string literal change in `lsp_build_reply`.
Drive already emits any non-empty payload. Drive needs no new C.

`lsp_load_src` already uses `&FsCap` and `read_file`.
Completion may reuse that load. Do not add `process_exec`.
Do not add a new capability token on `main`.

## 6. Prefix and `&`

`lsp_is_ident_char` accepts `_`, digit, and letter only.
It does not accept `&`.
`lsp_ident_at` on `&Fs` returns `Fs`.

The ship says: include a leading `&` in the prefix.
That is product string work in `cli/lsp_complete.oo`.
Read the char before the ident. If it is `&`, prepend `&`.
Do not change the oodac lexer. Do not add a C ident API.

`cli/lsp_ident.oo` is shared read-only on this ship.
Do not edit it. Hover of `add` vs `main` must stay as it is.

Empty prefix: `lsp_ident_at` returns `""` on space.
The catalog then returns the full list. That is not a hang.
That is not a crash. That is not a C change.

## 7. Emit of a new CLI file

`cli/lsp_reply.oo` has 220 lines. Room remains for one import and one branch.
If the file would pass 256 lines, split dispatch only.

`import "lsp_complete.oo"` from `cli/lsp_reply.oo` resolves with
`path_join(dir, imp)` in `oodac/load_import.oo`.
That is the live same-folder probe. No oodac edit.

`bootstrap/oodac_pure_build` emits `cli/main.oo` and links `chs_rt`.
It does not keep a C list of CLI files.
A new imported `.oo` file is spliced into the source. Then emit-c runs.

Stay on the name table in section 5.
If DE2 invents a new free name, seed emit fails as an unknown call.
That fail is not a reason to patch `chs_rt`.
Delete the new name. Use the table.

## 8. Emit fails that are not C

These errors are live import law. They are not missing C APIs.

1. `ERR import not found after relative probes ... lsp_types.oo`
   Cause: copy the unused catalog import into `cli/lsp_complete.oo`.
   Fix: drop that import. The resolve path does not use those types.

2. `ERR import path escape rejected: ../lsp/lsp_completion.oo`
   Cause: `reject_bad_import_name` rejects `..`.
   Fix: lift the catalog text. Do not import across folders.

3. `ERR import not found ... ooda/lsp/lsp_completion.oo`
   Cause: that folder does not exist in this worktree.
   Fix: read `lsp/lsp_completion.oo` as a catalog only. Do not import it.

4. Line-count fail from dinner_lint if a file exceeds 256 lines.
   Fix: keep the catalog in `cli/lsp_complete.oo`. Keep dispatch small.

None of these errors name a new C function.

